## 35. Trending Differentiation Features (Optional Enhancements)

These are current, high-impact ideas from leading automotive configurators (Porsche, BMW, Genesis-class experiences) that would make the product feel more attractive and shareable. They are optional layers on top of the core Definition of Done in §33, not required for launch.

### 35.1 High-Impact / Genuinely Trending

- **AR "View in your driveway"** (WebXR / `<model-viewer>` AR) — the user points their phone at a real space and the configured car appears life-size in it. Currently the single biggest "wow" feature in premium automotive configurators.
- **Dynamic environments** — let users place the finished build into different scenes (night city, coastal road, track, showroom) with matching lighting/reflections, showcasing paint metallic/pearl properties.
- **Sound design toggle** — engine start-up, door-close thud, ambient showroom audio on interaction. Low cost, disproportionately raises perceived quality.
- **Shareable video, not just image** — an auto-generated 3–5 second vertical orbit clip of the finished build, built for Instagram/TikTok sharing rather than a static screenshot.

### 35.2 Social / Community Layer

- **Public build gallery** — "Most Popular Builds This Week" with likes/remix, turning individual configuration into a social feed that drives return visits.
- **Rarity/achievement badges** — e.g. "Only 3% of users chose this paint + wheel combo," gamifying configuration without cheapening the brand.
- **Live collaborative build** — a shareable link that lets a friend join and configure the same build together in real time (Figma-style multiplayer cursors, applied to a car).

### 35.3 AI-Forward (extends the existing CarAI assistant)

- **Voice-driven CarAI** — spoken commands ("make it more aggressive") with the assistant narrating changes back, instead of typed-only input.
- **AI-generated concept renders** — an aspirational, clearly-labeled "dream concept" image of an even more extreme version of the build, positioned as inspiration rather than a purchasable configuration — a fun top-of-funnel hook.

### 35.4 Lower-Effort, Still Worth It

- **Before/after slider** on AI recommendations — drag to compare the current build against the AI-suggested one.
- **"Drive it" mini-mode** — a lightweight arcade-style camera fly-through/drive simulation on the finished build screen, purely for delight, not a real driving game.

