## 36. Authentication & Accounts

Several already-specified features implicitly require knowing who the user is — **Saved Builds** (§18, nav in §22), **shared configurations**, plus the newer **lead capture/reservations (§34.1)**, **public gallery with likes (§35.2)**, and **live collaborative build (§35.2)**. This section makes that explicit.

### 36.1 Login Page

- Email + password login.
- Optional social login (Google, Apple) — fits a premium-brand experience and reduces signup friction.
- "Forgot password?" link.
- Visually consistent with the rest of the site: dark background, glassmorphism panel, minimal fields, no clutter.

### 36.2 Sign-Up Page

- Name, email, password (with confirmation and strength indicator).
- Optional social sign-up (Google, Apple).
- Clear link back to Login for existing users.
- Terms of service / privacy policy checkbox (ties into §34.4 compliance).

### 36.3 Password Reset Flow

- "Forgot password" → email with a time-limited reset link → new password form.
- Standard security practices: reset tokens single-use and expiring, no user enumeration in error messages.

### 36.4 Account Dashboard ("My Garage")

- Lists the user's saved builds (from §18), with load/edit/delete actions.
- Shows submitted quote requests/reservations (from §34.1), if any.
- Shows the user's published gallery entries (from §35.2), if any.
- Basic profile settings: name, email, password change, connected social accounts.

### 36.5 Guest Mode

- Users can configure, price, and even locally save a build **without** creating an account.
- An account is only required at the point of: publishing to the public gallery, generating a permanent shareable link tied to an account, submitting a lead/reservation, or starting a live collaborative session.
- This keeps the core "wow" experience (§30) frictionless while still gating account-dependent features appropriately.

### 36.6 Navigation Update

- The nav bar (§22) gains an **Account** area on the right, alongside **AI Assistant** and **Saved Builds**: shows "Log In / Sign Up" when signed out, and the user's avatar/name (linking to "My Garage") when signed in.